-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- KnowledgeHoldings: Where a piece of a procedure's knowledge lives at one point in time (before and after encoding): operators' memory, formal documents, notes in outdated manuals, the memory of staff who may leave, unspoken crew agreements, or the procedure rulebook.
